Description: Import the GL scanout with its planes, offsets and modifier
 .
 Karton read the scanout through the single-plane API, which carries no
 modifier, and built the EGL image from the stride alone. A driver that
 tiles its buffers (NVIDIA's) then receives a buffer it reads as
 linear, and the guest's picture never shows.
 .
 Use spice_display_channel_get_gl_scanout2() and build the EGL
 attribute list the way spice-gtk's own EGL path does: every plane with
 its descriptor, pitch, offset and the buffer's modifier. Clear stale
 GL errors before binding the image so the check covers only the bind.
 .
 An import that fails now says so once per scanout (size, fourcc,
 modifier, planes, and whether Qt gave an EGL display) instead of
 leaving a blank view with a debug line.
